#: ../../peps/peps/pep-0756.rst:36
msgid ""
":pep:`393` \"Flexible String Representation\" changed string internals in "
"Python 3.3 to use three formats:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../peps/peps/pep-0756.rst:39
msgid ""
"``PyUnicode_1BYTE_KIND``: Unicode range [U+0000; U+00ff], UCS-1, 1 byte/"
"character."
msgstr ""

#: ../../peps/peps/pep-0756.rst:41
msgid ""
"``PyUnicode_2BYTE_KIND``: Unicode range [U+0000; U+ffff], UCS-2, 2 bytes/"
"character."
msgstr ""

#: ../../peps/peps/pep-0756.rst:43
msgid ""
"``PyUnicode_4BYTE_KIND``: Unicode range [U+0000; U+10ffff], UCS-4, 4 bytes/"
"character."
msgstr ""

#: ../../peps/peps/pep-0756.rst:46
msgid ""
"A Python ``str`` object must always use the most compact format. For "
"example, a string which only contains ASCII characters must use the UCS-1 "
"format."
msgstr ""

#: ../../peps/peps/pep-0756.rst:50
msgid ""
"The ``PyUnicode_KIND()`` function can be used to know the format used by a "
"string."
msgstr ""

