#: ../../peps/peps/pep-0756.rst:329
msgid "Rejected Ideas"
msgstr ""

#: ../../peps/peps/pep-0756.rst:332
msgid "Reject embedded NUL characters and require trailing NUL character"
msgstr ""

#: ../../peps/peps/pep-0756.rst:334
msgid ""
"In C, it's convenient to have a trailing NUL character. For example, the "
"``for (; *str != 0; str++)`` loop can be used to iterate on characters and "
"``strlen()`` can be used to get a string length."
msgstr ""

#: ../../peps/peps/pep-0756.rst:338
msgid ""
"The problem is that a Python ``str`` object can embed NUL characters. "
"Example: ``\"ab\\0c\"``. If a string contains an embedded NUL character, "
"code relying on the NUL character to find the string end truncates the "
"string. It can lead to bugs, or even security vulnerabilities. See a "
"previous discussion in the issue `Change PyUnicode_AsUTF8() to return NULL "
"on embedded null characters <https://github.com/python/cpython/"
"issues/111089>`_."
msgstr ""

#: ../../peps/peps/pep-0756.rst:346
msgid ""
"Rejecting embedded NUL characters require to scan the string which has an "
"*O*\\ (*n*) complexity."
msgstr ""

#: ../../peps/peps/pep-0756.rst:351
msgid "Reject surrogate characters"
msgstr ""

#: ../../peps/peps/pep-0756.rst:353
msgid ""
"Surrogate characters are characters in the Unicode range [U+D800; U+DFFF].  "
"They are disallowed by UTF codecs such as UTF-8. A Python ``str`` object can "
"contain arbitrary lone surrogate characters. Example: ``\"\\uDC80\"``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../peps/peps/pep-0756.rst:358
msgid ""
"Rejecting surrogate characters prevents exporting a string which contains "
"such a character. It can be surprising and annoying since the "
"``PyUnicode_Export()`` caller doesn't control the string contents."
msgstr ""

#: ../../peps/peps/pep-0756.rst:362
msgid ""
"Allowing surrogate characters allows to export any string and so avoid this "
"issue. For example, the UTF-8 codec can be used with the ``surrogatepass`` "
"error handler to encode and decode surrogate characters."
msgstr ""

#: ../../peps/peps/pep-0756.rst:369
msgid "Conversions on demand"
msgstr ""

#: ../../peps/peps/pep-0756.rst:371
msgid ""
"It would be convenient to convert formats on demand. For example, convert "
"UCS-1 and UCS-2 to UCS-4 if an export to only UCS-4 is requested."
msgstr ""

#: ../../peps/peps/pep-0756.rst:375
msgid ""
"The problem is that most users expect an export to require no memory copy "
"and no conversion: an *O*\\ (1) complexity. It is better to have an API "
"where all operations have an *O*\\ (1) complexity."
msgstr ""

#: ../../peps/peps/pep-0756.rst:380
msgid "Export to UTF-8"
msgstr ""

#: ../../peps/peps/pep-0756.rst:382
msgid ""
"CPython 3.14 has a cache to encode a string to UTF-8. It is tempting to "
"allow exporting to UTF-8."
msgstr ""

#: ../../peps/peps/pep-0756.rst:385
msgid ""
"The problem is that the UTF-8 cache doesn't support surrogate characters. An "
"export is expected to provide the whole string content, including embedded "
"NUL characters and surrogate characters. To export surrogate characters, a "
"different code path using the ``surrogatepass`` error handler is needed and "
"each export operation has to allocate a temporary buffer: *O*\\ (n) "
"complexity."
msgstr ""

#: ../../peps/peps/pep-0756.rst:392
msgid ""
"An export is expected to have an *O*\\ (1) complexity, so the idea to export "
"UTF-8 in CPython was abadonned."
msgstr ""

#: ../../peps/peps/pep-0756.rst:397
